  "text": "让我们从这个数字系统开始，知道它有base $b$。我们需要找到这个代表哪个数字系统。我们可以通过比较这个数的各个部分，确定其大小，从而推断出相同的Digits > 1.的形式。\n\n我们将先求出右边的Two-digit数，也是整数个位数。因此，我们首先将求的数字减去One-letter数，从而得到0。这意味着，右边的Map of digits的中间两个槽已填充完毕。\n\n现在，我们可以比较左边的Three-digit数和右边的Two-digit数。由于左边的Three-digit数已经填满，并且右边的Two-digit数已知，这就是我们将要解决的部分。\n\n在valid解法过程中，留下的是未解决的Two-letter数。我们还没有确定这个拨盘上的$X$，但需要注意$X \\geq 2$，也就是说，该数将仅使用两个字母编号。\n\n如果$a$是已知的数字（或者数字），我们会进行一些独立的计算（注意到其中有一个左侧待确认的数位），然后将它带回到方程中，求出该数位的值。\n\n因此最初计算的意义是把所有数值拆分并放置在一个可分配的组中，对所有的数值执行.\n\n\">-->\n  [compatibility]  [compatibility]\nThe above is a picture from Wikipedia which connects two numbers because there are dots between them. The number of dots is between 2 and 10 indicating the number of X in the corresponding Y-* digit.\n\">-->\n  [compatibility]  [compatibility]\nFor our case, we are using Numbers to represent X. According to the schematic, the picture represents numbers which are not greater than 10 because there are 10 dots between 2 and 10.\n\nTherefore, the valid range is $2 \\leq a,b \\leq 10$.\n\">-->\n  [compatibility]  [compatibility]\n-->\n  [gaps]  [gaps]\nNow, let us visualize the blocks. The number of blocks between two numbers tells us the number of $g (g = X, g = Y)$ in the corresponding $f (f = A, f = B, f = C, \\ldots)$digit. \n\nIf we treat $g (g = X)$ as an integer-coordinate slope, we can call the sloping block$(X)$ as the shaded block. Then, $b$ is the sum of the horizontal and vertical distances between the two coordinates.\n\nHere are the slightly different slanting blocks:\n\n($f = C, g = B$)$(f = A, g = B)$\n\n(see number 4 page 77)\n\n($f = B, g = A$)$(f = B, g = D)$\n\nIn our case, $b = 7 + 3 + 1 + 2 + 2 = 17$, which is a valid base which satisfies the conditions.\n\nTherefore, $b = 17$.\n-->\n  [calculation]  [calculation]\nBut actually, there are three different ways to prove number 4:\n\nIf we treat thex-coordinate of block $(C \\to A)$, the slanting path of base$(17)$, which is composed of these twoslants, as shown in the right picture, thiscan be solved uniquely.\n\n\nTo correctly reason, we should first define thatthe path must beequal to the sum of the horizontal and vertical distances between the two coordinates (The number of dots is between 2 and 10 indicating the number of X in the corresponding Y-* digit).\n\n把所有的计算结果进行累积。\n\">-->\n  [calculation]  [calculation]\nTherefore, the valid range is $2 \\leq X \\leq 10$.",
